=== SURVEY ===
Web source AIChatbotIndicator.tsx = `withAiFeature('chatbot-llm', InnerIndicator)`.
  • InnerIndicator: a single inline cyan chip — `<HelixMark/>` + `t('helix.badge','Helix')`, with
    `title={t('helix.tooltip', 'Helix is your AI assistant. It generates responses using your
    redacted fleet context.')}` and `aria-label={t('helix.ariaLabel','Helix')}`.
  • withAiFeature → useAiEnabled('chatbot-llm') truth table (ADR-015 AI-Off, fail-closed):
    enabled IFF AI_FEATURES['chatbot-llm'] exists AND settings resolved AND
    settings.ai_mode ∉ {undefined,'off'} AND settings.ai_features['chatbot-llm'] === true; every
    other state (query unresolved, errored, mode off, flag off/missing) → `false` → renders `null`.
Data sources (P1/S8): useTranslation (gate folds useSettings). Shared components: HelixMark,
withAiFeature. Charts/maps: none. Canonical surface pattern studied: shared-surfaces/
AIAutoTripNameSuggestion (Adapter/Model/Seams/Views/States/Previews/strings/Tests/ModelTests) +
the exact-surface predecessor slot-241 artifact log (Adapter/Projection/Model/Views/swift/Previews/
strings/Tests).

=== REASONING ===
- The native surface reproduces the web composition: a fail-closed AI-Off gate that withdraws the
  surface entirely when the feature is off, and renders the cyan Helix badge when it is on — bound
  through `AIChatbotIndicatorModel` (no HTTP/settings read in the view).
- Architecture (mirrors the canonical leaf + the exact-surface predecessor):
  • Adapter (pure, Foundation): AIChatbotConnection (P4 freshness axis), AIChatbotSettingsStatus
    (web useSettings lifecycle), AIChatbotMode (web settings.ai_mode), AIChatbotIndicatorInput,
    AIChatbotGate (verbatim useAiEnabled('chatbot-llm') truth-table port: evaluate() →
    unresolved/failed/disabled/enabled + isPresented/isEnabled boolean parity),
    AIChatbotIndicatorMeta (featureID='chatbot-llm', surfaceSlug='AIChatbotIndicator'),
    AIChatbotAccessibility (freshness-aware badge label).
  • Projection (pure): AIChatbotResolved + resolve() → gatedOff / loading / unavailable / presented,
    carrying the connection axis.
  • Model: AIChatbotTelemetry seam (P1/S11 view.opened) + OSLog default; AIChatbotIndicatorSource
    seam (+Live host-binding / InMemory double); @Observable AIChatbotIndicatorModel — recomputes
    the projection, emits view.opened exactly once when the badge first presents (never while
    gated/loading), one-shot stale auto-refresh re-armed on return to live, offline never
    auto-refreshes; AIChatbotStrings i18n facade (table "AIChatbotIndicator").
  • Views: AIChatbotHelixMark(+Shape) — the VERBATIM port of the web HelixMark SVG (strand A
    `M 8 2 Q 18 7 12 12 Q 6 17 16 22`, strand B mirrored, rungs at y=7/y=17) as a stroked SwiftUI
    Shape; AIChatbotBadge (cyan chip, tooltip via .help, freshness-aware a11y); AIChatbotFreshnessDot
    (tappable refresh); AIChatbotLoadingChip (neutral TSSkeleton pill); AIChatbotUnavailableChip
    (neutral TSButton retry). Reuses the shared TSSkeleton/TSButton + P1/S9 tokens.
  • swift (surface entry: gatedOff → EmptyView else phase-routed content); Previews (per state);
    Tests (XCTest); strings.
- The `withAiFeature` gate is reproduced faithfully: feature off (disabled) → the surface renders
  NOTHING (ADR-015 AI-Off — the gate exists precisely so no AI surface leaks). The P4 "every state
  renders, never a blank box" rule is honoured WITHOUT leaking the gate verdict: the two non-terminal
  settings states render NEUTRAL chrome (a shimmer pill while loading, a no-branding retry chip on
  settings failure) that carries no Helix/AI branding and collapses to nothing if the gate resolves
  off. The presented badge is the content state; stale/offline decorate it with the freshness axis.
- Naming: the mark is `AIChatbotHelixMark` (NOT the bare `HelixMark`) because a sibling surface
  (AIAutoTripNameSuggestion.Views) already declares an internal `HelixMark` in the single app module
  — a second `HelixMark` would be a real duplicate-type error introduced by THIS surface. Self-named
  → 0 collisions (covenant 7/8).
- Rejected: porting the web Tailwind/`null` literally as a hidden surface for loading/error (the P4
  leaf contract requires visible chrome — rendered neutrally); reusing the sibling's internal
  HelixMark (cross-surface coupling + the allowed-files restriction); a settings read in the view
  (routed through the source seam); emitting view.opened on mount (the web `null` while gated means
  the surface was never opened — emitted lazily on first present).

